To implement an end-to-end program execution pipeline that compiles source code to runtime backend objects and runs the compiled program, you will need to follow several steps. Below is a structured approach to help you complete the assignment.

### Step 1: Define the Grammar in ANTLR

You will need to create a grammar file `PL.g4` in the `src` directory. This grammar should support the minimal features required to run the four programs provided in your worksheet. 

Here’s a basic example of what your grammar might look like:

```antlr
grammar PL;

program: statement* EOF;

statement
    : assignment
    | printStatement
    ;

assignment
    : ID '=' expression ';'
    ;

printStatement
    : 'print' '(' expression ')' ';'
    ;

expression
    : ID
    | INT
    | expression '+' expression
    | expression '-' expression
    | expression '*' expression
    | expression '/' expression
    ;

ID: [a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*;
INT: [0-9]+;
WS: [ \t\r\n]+ -> skip;
```

### Step 2: Implement Kotlin Classes

In the `src/backend.kt` file, you will need to implement several Kotlin classes. Here’s a breakdown of what you might need:

1. **Compiled Runtime Backend Objects**: These classes will represent the compiled objects that can be executed at runtime.

```kotlin
data class CompiledProgram(val instructions: List<Instruction>)

sealed class Instruction {
    data class Print(val value: String) : Instruction()
    data class Assign(val id: String, val value: Int) : Instruction()
    // Add more instructions as needed
}
```

2. **Visitor Class for Compilation**: This class will traverse the parse tree generated by ANTLR and compile the source code into runtime objects.

```kotlin
import org.antlr.v4.runtime.tree.ParseTreeVisitor

class CompilerVisitor : PLBaseVisitor<CompiledProgram>() {
    private val instructions = mutableListOf<Instruction>()

    override fun visitAssignment(ctx: PLParser.AssignmentContext): CompiledProgram {
        val id = ctx.ID().text
        val value = visit(ctx.expression())
        instructions.add(Instruction.Assign(id, value))
        return CompiledProgram(instructions)
    }

    override fun visitPrintStatement(ctx: PLParser.PrintStatementContext): CompiledProgram {
        val value = visit(ctx.expression())
        instructions.add(Instruction.Print(value.toString()))
        return CompiledProgram(instructions)
    }

    // Implement other visit methods as needed
}
```

### Step 3: Implement the Main Execution Pipeline

You will need a main function that ties everything together: parsing the input, compiling it, and executing the compiled instructions.

```kotlin
fun main(args: Array<String>) {
    val input = "your source code here" // Replace with actual input
    val lexer = PLLexer(CharStreams.fromString(input))
    val tokens = CommonTokenStream(lexer)
    val parser = PLParser(tokens)

    val tree = parser.program()
    val compiler = CompilerVisitor()
    val compiledProgram = compiler.visit(tree)

    // Execute the compiled program
    execute(compiledProgram)
}

fun execute(compiledProgram: CompiledProgram) {
    for (instruction in compiledProgram.instructions) {
        when (instruction) {
            is Instruction.Print -> println(instruction.value)
            is Instruction.Assign -> {
                // Handle assignment logic
            }
        }
    }
}
```

### Step 4: Makefile

Ensure your `Makefile` is set up to compile your Kotlin code and run the program. Here’s a simple example:

```makefile
KOTLINC = kotlinc
KOTLINC_FLAGS = -cp .:antlr-4.9.2-complete.jar

all: compile run

compile:
	$(KOTLINC) $(KOTLINC_FLAGS) src/*.kt -d out

run:
	kotlin -cp out MainKt
```

### Step 5: Testing

Make sure to test your implementation with the four programs provided in your worksheet. Adjust the grammar and Kotlin classes as necessary to ensure compatibility.

### Conclusion

This structured approach should help you implement the end-to-end program execution pipeline. Make sure to adapt the code snippets to fit the specific requirements of your assignment and the features of the language you are implementing.

