Below is a simple HTML structure that meets your requirements. This code assumes you have a `countries.json` file that contains the necessary data about countries, including their names, flags, demographics, area, and population. The JavaScript part will handle the fetching of the JSON data, updating the display based on user selection, and converting area units.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Country Information</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            margin: 20px;
        }
        #country-info {
            margin-top: 20px;
        }
        img {
            max-width: 200px;
            height: auto;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <h1>Select a Country</h1>
    <select id="country-select">
        <option value="">--Select a Country--</option>
    </select>

    <div id="country-info" style="display: none;">
        <h2 id="country-name"></h2>
        <img id="country-flag" alt="Country Flag">
        <p><strong>Population:</strong> <span id="country-population"></span></p>
        <p><strong>Total Area:</strong> <span id="country-area"></span> <span id="area-unit">square miles</span></p>
        <p><strong>Population Density:</strong> <span id="population-density"></span> <span id="density-unit">per square mile</span></p>

        <label for="area-unit-select">Change Area Unit:</label>
        <select id="area-unit-select">
            <option value="miles">Square Miles</option>
            <option value="kilometers">Square Kilometers</option>
        </select>

        <button id="wiki-button" style="margin-top: 20px;">Wiki Country</button>
    </div>

    <script>
        let countries = [];

        // Fetch countries data from countries.json
        fetch('countries.json')
            .then(response => response.json())
            .then(data => {
                countries = data;
                const select = document.getElementById('country-select');
                countries.forEach(country => {
                    const option = document.createElement('option');
                    option.value = country.name;
                    option.textContent = country.name;
                    select.appendChild(option);
                });
            });

        document.getElementById('country-select').addEventListener('change', function() {
            const selectedCountry = countries.find(country => country.name === this.value);
            if (selectedCountry) {
                document.getElementById('country-name').textContent = selectedCountry.name;
                document.getElementById('country-flag').src = selectedCountry.flag;
                document.getElementById('country-population').textContent = selectedCountry.population;
                updateAreaDisplay(selectedCountry.area, 'miles');
                document.getElementById('country-info').style.display = 'block';
                document.getElementById('wiki-button').onclick = () => {
                    window.open(`https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/${selectedCountry.name}`, '_blank');
                };
            } else {
                document.getElementById('country-info').style.display = 'none';
            }
        });

        document.getElementById('area-unit-select').addEventListener('change', function() {
            const selectedCountry = countries.find(country => country.name === document.getElementById('country-select').value);
            if (selectedCountry) {
                updateAreaDisplay(selectedCountry.area, this.value);
            }
        });

        function updateAreaDisplay(area, unit) {
            let areaValue = area;
            let densityValue = (area > 0) ? (selectedCountry.population / area) : 0;

            if (unit === 'kilometers') {
                areaValue = area * 2.58999; // Convert square miles to square kilometers
                densityValue = (areaValue > 0) ? (selectedCountry.population / areaValue) : 0;
                document.getElementById('density-unit').textContent = 'per square kilometer';
            } else {
                document.getElementById('density-unit').textContent = 'per square mile';
            }

            document.getElementById('country-area').textContent = areaValue.toFixed(2);
            document.getElementById('area-unit').textContent = unit === 'kilometers' ? 'square kilometers' : 'square miles';
            document.getElementById('population-density').textContent = densityValue.toFixed(2);
        }
    </script>

</body>
</html>
```

### Explanation:
1. **HTML Structure**: The HTML includes a dropdown for country selection, a section to display country information, and a button to open the Wikipedia page.
2. **CSS Styles**: Basic styles are applied for better readability.
3. **JavaScript**:
   - Fetches country data from `countries.json`.
   - Populates the dropdown with country names.
   - Displays country information when a country is selected.
   - Updates area and population density based on the selected unit.
   - Opens the Wikipedia page in a new tab when the button is clicked.

### Note:
- Ensure that the `countries.json` file is structured correctly and accessible from the same directory or adjust the fetch path accordingly.
- The area and population density calculations assume that the area is provided in square miles in the JSON file. Adjust the conversion logic if the data format is different.

