Creating a custom OBS (Open Broadcaster Software) QSS theme using gradients, colors, and fonts can give your streaming setup a unique look. Below is a sample QSS (Qt Style Sheet) that incorporates purple and blue gradients, the Montserrat Alternates font, and other design elements inspired by DOS branding.

### Sample QSS Theme for OBS

```css
/* Set the overall font for the application */
* {
    font-family: 'Montserrat Alternates', sans-serif;
}

/* Main Window */
QMainWindow {
    background: qlineargradient(x1:0, y1:0, x2:1, y2:1, stop:0 #4B0082, stop:1 #1E90FF);
    color: #FFFFFF;
}

/* Title Bar */
QWidget#titleBar {
    background: qlineargradient(x1:0, y1:0, x2:1, y2:1, stop:0 #6A5ACD, stop:1 #00BFFF);
    color: #FFFFFF;
}

/* Buttons */
QPushButton {
    background-color: #6A5ACD;
    border: 2px solid #1E90FF;
    border-radius: 5px;
    padding: 5px;
    color: #FFFFFF;
}

QPushButton:hover {
    background-color: #1E90FF;
}

/* Text Fields */
QLineEdit, QTextEdit {
    background-color: #FFFFFF;
    border: 2px solid #6A5ACD;
    border-radius: 5px;
    padding: 5px;
    color: #000000;
}

/* Combo Boxes */
QComboBox {
    background-color: #FFFFFF;
    border: 2px solid #6A5ACD;
    border-radius: 5px;
    padding: 5px;
}

/* Scroll Bars */
QScrollBar:vertical {
    background: #6A5ACD;
    width: 10px;
}

QScrollBar::handle:vertical {
    background: #1E90FF;
    min-height: 20px;
}

QScrollBar::add-line:vertical, QScrollBar::sub-line:vertical {
    background: none;
}

/* Labels */
QLabel {
    color: #FFFFFF;
}

/* Checkboxes */
QCheckBox {
    color: #FFFFFF;
}

QCheckBox::indicator {
    background-color: #6A5ACD;
    border: 2px solid #1E90FF;
}

QCheckBox::indicator:checked {
    background-color: #1E90FF;
}

/* Radio Buttons */
QRadioButton {
    color: #FFFFFF;
}

QRadioButton::indicator {
    background-color: #6A5ACD;
    border: 2px solid #1E90FF;
}

QRadioButton::indicator:checked {
    background-color: #1E90FF;
}

/* Progress Bars */
QProgressBar {
    background-color: #6A5ACD;
    border: 2px solid #1E90FF;
    border-radius: 5px;
}

QProgressBar::chunk {
    background-color: #1E90FF;
}

/* Tooltips */
QToolTip {
    background-color: #1E90FF;
    color: #FFFFFF;
    border: 1px solid #6A5ACD;
    padding: 5px;
}
```

### Instructions to Use the QSS Theme in OBS

1. **Install Montserrat Alternates Font**: Make sure you have the Montserrat Alternates font installed on your system. You can download it from Google Fonts or other font repositories.

2. **Open OBS**: Launch OBS Studio.

3. **Access Settings**: Go to `File` > `Settings`.

4. **Go to the "General" Tab**: In the settings window, navigate to the "General" tab.

5. **Custom CSS**: Look for the option to add custom CSS or QSS. This may vary based on the version of OBS you are using.

6. **Paste the QSS Code**: Copy the QSS code provided above and paste it into the custom CSS/QSS field.

7. **Apply and Restart**: Click `OK` or `Apply`, and then restart OBS to see the changes take effect.

### Customization

Feel free to adjust the colors, gradients, and other properties to better fit your personal style or branding. You can also add more elements or modify existing ones based on your preferences. Enjoy your new OBS theme!

